# Public API

## Facade (JS/PHP parity)

```dart
await Talaria.init(TalariaOptions(...));
Talaria.logger(name: …, tags: …, minLevel: …);
Talaria.withTags({…});
Talaria.debug/info/warning/warn/error/fatal(message, {context});
Talaria.log(level, message, {context});
Talaria.captureException(error, {stackTrace, context});
Talaria.captureMessage(message, {level, context});
Talaria.getMinLevel(); Talaria.setMinLevel(level); Talaria.isLevelEnabled(level);
Talaria.isEnforceDefaultLevel(); Talaria.setEnforceDefaultLevel(bool);
Talaria.flush();
Talaria.close();
```

Also export `TalariaClient` for DI and `TalariaLogger` for scoped capture.
Flutter: `TalariaFlutter.init`, `TalariaFlutter.runZonedApp`, `TalariaNavigatorObserver`.

## Init options

- Required: `dsn` or `baseUrl`, `apiKey`, `environment`
- Optional: `release`, `commitSha`, `sampleRate`, `minLevel` (default `debug`), `enforceDefaultLevel` (default `false`), `loggers`, `beforeSend`, `maxBatchSize`, `flushIntervalMs`, `defaultIntegrations`, `userId`, `tags`, `httpTimeoutSeconds`, `platform`

## Capture rules

- Exceptions default `level: error`; messages default `info`
- Derive `eventType` from level
- Context bag: `tags`, `extra`, `userId`, `title`, optional `mechanism`
- Gates: effective level → `sampleRate` → `beforeSend`; filtered captures are quiet no-ops
- Capture enqueues only — network I/O happens on queue drain
